    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Isaac Paredes** (70.39) as our premier offensive anchor. Facing G. Rodriguez, **Isaac Paredes** benefits from an elite SP matchup (4.64 xERA) and a favorable #3 hole placement, providing the ideal setup to maximize counting stats. While he anchors the lineup, we are also leaning heavily into our speed-first strategy at the top of the order. Both **Brice Turang** (61.75) and **Henry Bolte** (61.38) are cleared for duty against Dobnak; their high-leadoff placement, combined with a significant SP skill advantage, makes them primary targets for SB accumulation. **Max Muncy** (60.01) rounds out our 60+ tier, leveraging his excellent SP matchup to offset his platoon disadvantage.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was leaving **Vinnie Pasquantino** (51.00) on the bench. Despite his solid underlying projections, he was squeezed out by a combination of the platoon disadvantage against the lefty Jump and the superior lineup efficiency afforded to the rest of the infield. We are keeping a close eye on **Jose Caballero**, whose high park factor (16%) is currently dampened by a poor #9 batting order slot. His scoring (54.79) remains marginal, but he remains our primary contingency if we need to chase stolen bases late in the day. We are continuing to monitor the health of **James Wood** and **Tyler Soderstrom**, both of whom remain sidelined on the IL, limiting our depth as we navigate the final stretch of the season. \n\nWe are avoiding any high-risk exposure to elite arms today, though **Josh Naylor** (56.41) and **Austin Riley** (56.97) represent our most precarious plays. **Austin Riley** is currently suffering from a severe \"order penalty\" due to his #8 positioning, which severely limits his R and RBI potential despite a favorable matchup against Kay. As we continue to balance our daily efficiency scores with our season-long game cap management, we are content to bench **Cole Young** and others in favor of the optimized matchups for **Travis Bazzana** and the middle-infield cohort. We will be closely monitoring the status of **Corbin Carroll**, **Mickey Moniak**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Trevor Story**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Griffin Conine**, and **Edwin Arroyo** to ensure our bench remains ready for a late-slate pivot.",
